---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="AZIZFITNESS | Member Portal">
    <section class="section section-light">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header">
          <span class="eyebrow">Member Portal</span>
          <h2>Coming soon: your training, nutrition, booking and progress hub</h2>
          <p>This portal will eventually give members secure access to personalized plans, schedules, and progress tracking.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="resource-grid">
          <article class="resource-card"><h4>Dashboard</h4><p>One place for training goals, progress, and announcements.</p></article>
          <article class="resource-card"><h4>Workout Plans</h4><p>Personalized sessions that match your program.</p></article>
          <article class="resource-card"><h4>Nutrition</h4><p>Meal plans, recipes, and coaching notes.</p></article>
          <article class="resource-card"><h4>Booking</h4><p>Reserve classes, training sessions, and recovery appointments.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-dark">
      <div class="container section-split reverse">
        <div class="section-image">
          <img src="/coaches.jpg" alt="Portal preview" loading="lazy">
        </div>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <span class="eyebrow">Platform roadmap</span>
          <h2>Build the foundation for a fitness platform</h2>
          <p>Start with a public marketing site and expand into a member experience without changing the brand look and feel.</p>
          <div class="feature-list">
            <div><strong>Member dashboard</strong><p>Track workouts, bookings, and progress in one place.</p></div>
            <div><strong>Coach tools</strong><p>Manage clients, sessions, and program notes.</p></div>
            <div><strong>Growth-ready</strong><p>Design the site to support future subscriptions and access tiers.</p></div>
          </div>
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Ask about the portal</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
</Layout>
